WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
The cicada situation is out of control

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.680
Oh good morning Hank, it's Tuesday, so when we last visited the garden

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.020
it was mostly dirt

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.380
but now there are zucchini and sunflowers and these weird dragon tongue beans.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.040
We've got eggplants and oregano

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.240
and most of all we have tomatoes

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.040
We've got  black cherry tomatoes, we've got red cherry tomatoes, we've got these weird guys

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.940
and we've also got a metric crap ton of golden currants

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.380
which are tiny little tomatoes not much larger than a pea.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.020
Why did I get so many tomato plants that make tiny tomatoes?

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.880
Because I wanna eat 211 tomatoes in a single sitting.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.180
One, two...

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.100
Five... This is gonna take a while

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.420
I have picked the tomatoes. It took thirty four minutes and I am drenched in sweat.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.600
Let's go inside

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.040
Actually you know what, before we go, picking all of these tomatoes has made me wanna eat a tomato

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.280
So I'm going to, hold on

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.880
Mmm, delicious

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.440
I'm gonna have another one

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.640
Mmm. New video title, "How to Eat 213 Tomatoes in a Single Sitting"

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.800
Okay so the first thing you're gonna want to do is lay out your bountiful harvest

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:01.820
and then consider all of the time, energy and sweat that went into the creation of this 900 calories of food.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.480
Then, give thanks to actual farm workers

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:09.900
And then count out exactly 211 tomatoes because people on the internet are sticklers about that stuff

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.740
So today we're going to make panzanella

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.080
which is essentially tomatoes with croutons.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.720
To make the croutons you wanna preheat the oven to 350 degrees,

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.200
being careful not to look at your ghoulish reflection

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.800
Then take a pan, tear up some good bread, put it in four-ish cloves of minced garlic, some olive oil

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:25.480
and then I think the technical term is you just

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:26.560
sort of 'hoosh' it.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:31.280
And then once it's adequately 'hooshed' put it in the oven and cook it for, I don't know, like 15 minutes

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.440
Then you're gonna want to chop up all of your non-golden currant tomatoes

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:35.260
and

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:35.880
boom

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:39.980
It was at this point that I realised that even 211 small tomatoes

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.000
is still a lot of tomatoes

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.520
I googled "can eating too many tomatoes kill you?"

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.820
and it turns out, probably not, but it can turn your skin orange

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.400
Incidentally, you may not think you like tomatoes.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.440
I thought I hated them until my late twenties

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.140
but it turned out I had just never had a good one.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.780
Tomatoes are one of the very few foods where the good version

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:01.140
is essentially like a different thing than the bad version

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.640
Another example would be the difference between actual Lucky Charms and knock off Lucky Charms

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.400
So lets go back to the recipe

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.840
So you wanna put all your tomatoes in a large bowl, add some balsamic vinegar

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.300
less olive oil than I just used, some salt and pepper

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.600
and then, 'hoosh'.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:19.060
The secret to panzanella is the crunch of the croutons combined with the juicyness of the tomatoes

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:20.940
So it doesn't keep well once mixed.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:26.140
If you want leftovers, you need to keep them separate and then add them together as you go.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:29.340
So once your croutons are toasty, mix a handful with a handful of tomatoes

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:33.100
put some sliced basil on the top and you've got yourself an excellent meal.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.860
I ate around a hundred tomatoes at lunch

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:37.320
and then Sarah and I split the remaining tomatoes at dinner

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:41.000
Three great meals and my skin did not even turn orange

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.500
Now I just gotta figure out what to do with those zucchini

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.205
Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

